      <h2>Side projects</h2>

      <p>
        <strong>Wabi Sabi Interview News Archive.</strong> A daily business-news digest built
        for Indian B-school students preparing for placement interviews. Every entry pairs
        the story with the thing an interviewer would actually push on — why a PMI dip above
        50 reads differently from a contraction, where comparative advertising stops being
        comparison and becomes disparagement, what a late entrant buying its way into
        quick-commerce says about scale economics.
      </p>

      <p>
        It is categorised across Finance, Marketing, Operations, Product Management and
        Consulting, and archived by day. The interesting part was not the summarising — it
        was deciding what makes a news item <em>useful</em> under interview conditions, which
        turns out to be a much narrower filter than "important".
      </p>

